# The demo: /opt/injishi-demo/.env on the VPS, read by docker-compose.demo.yml
# and by demo-nightly.sh (ADR-043). Replace every change-me. Never reuse a
# production or staging secret here: the demo signs anyone in with a published
# code, so everything in this file should be assumed readable by a stranger.
# Generate secrets with: openssl rand -base64 32
#
# What is NOT here, on purpose: INJISHI_ENVIRONMENT and INJISHI_DATABASE_KIND
# (pinned as literals in the compose file), the adapter modes (pinned to mock),
# and any SMTP relay (every message goes to this stack's Mailpit).

# --- Hosts ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# The defaults are the demo hosts DOKPLOY.md lists; set these only to move them.
# WEB_HOST=www-demo.injishi.com
# APP_HOST=app-demo.injishi.com
# API_HOST=api-demo.injishi.com
# ADMIN_HOST=admin-demo.injishi.com
# STORAGE_HOST=storage-demo.injishi.com
# MAIL_HOST=mail-demo.injishi.com

# Who may open admin-demo and the Mailpit inbox (comma separated IPs or CIDRs).
# Unset means loopback only, which closes both.
ADMIN_ALLOWED_IPS=change-me

# --- Postgres (db service) --------------------------------------------------------
# The live database is always named injishi_demo; the nightly job builds the
# next one as injishi_demo_next beside it and renames at the swap, so
# DATABASE_URL must end in /injishi_demo. The password sits inside that URL:
# generate it as hex (openssl rand -hex 24), because base64's / + = are not
# valid in a URL unless percent encoded.
POSTGRES_USER=injishi
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=change-me
DATABASE_URL=postgres://injishi:change-me@db:5432/injishi_demo

# --- API and worker ---------------------------------------------------------------
COOKIE_SECRET=change-me
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=change-me
# Sandbox credentials only, if any.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
LOG_LEVEL=info
# The injishi-api DSN (a public, send only key). Empty leaves error reporting
# off; set, money alarms and what breaks reach Sentry under `demo` (ADR-063).
SENTRY_DSN=

# --- Object storage (minio, minio-init, API and worker) -----------------------------
# Every value its own. Signed URLs name storage-demo.injishi.com.
MINIO_ROOT_USER=injishi
MINIO_ROOT_PASSWORD=change-me
# <key-name>:<base64 of 32 random bytes>. Losing it only loses a day of demo
# uploads, which the nightly job empties anyway, but it is still never shared:
#   echo "injishi-demo-key:$(openssl rand -base64 32)"
MINIO_KMS_SECRET_KEY=change-me
STORAGE_BUCKET=injishi
STORAGE_S3_ACCESS_KEY=injishi-api
STORAGE_S3_SECRET_KEY=change-me
